{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3441","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3441","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3441\",\"parent_revision\":\"7aea190930e6323c88707ecd6505504bf8a55495ec0f692ff52b8566a35de72d\",\"root_revision\":\"7aea190930e6323c88707ecd6505504bf8a55495ec0f692ff52b8566a35de72d\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA repo-wide sweep of every plugin's runtime files found 200 references that resolve only in this repository. plugin-creator carries 38, which is notable because this is the plugin that ships the rule.\\n\\nAn escape is a path, markdown link, or cross-plugin mention in a plugin's runtime files (skills/ and agents/) that points outside the plugin that ships it. An installed consumer does not have this repository, so the reference resolves for the author alone and silently fails for everyone else.\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n\\n    uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py \\\\\\n        --plugin-dir plugins/plugin-creator\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nEach escape is an instruction an agent cannot follow once the plugin is installed anywhere but here. The failure is silent: the agent reads a path, finds nothing, and continues without the guidance the reference was meant to supply.\\n\\nThe plugin that documents the runtime-versus-design-time rule and ships the scanner enforcing it does not pass its own check. That is a credibility problem as well as a correctness one.\\n\\nKNOWN SHAPE OF THE REMAINDER\\n\\nMost of this plugin's escapes are SOURCE: lines citing a local path \u2014 other plugins' skill files, research/, examples/. These sit at the intersection of two repo rules: citations are required, and runtime text may not carry paths that only resolve here. Both are satisfiable. The citation rule asks skill derivations to link to the source repository, which is a URL that resolves everywhere and which the scanner does not flag. One citation in this plugin already does this correctly. The remedy is therefore per-citation: an external derivation becomes a URL, and provenance for an internal cross-plugin reference moves to the plugin's design-time notes.\\n\\nSWEEP CONTEXT\\n\\n200 escapes across 12 plugins; 17 of 29 are already clean. Counts: the-rewrite-room 40, plugin-creator 38, python-engineering 36, development-harness 32, python3-development 31, agentskill-kaizen 7, scientific-method 7, fastmcp-creator 3, orchestrator-discipline 3, agent-orchestration 1, perl-development 1, summarizer 1.\\n\\nThe scanner covers skills/ and agents/ only, so commands/, plugin-root CLAUDE.md, plugin-root references/ and docs/ are unscanned and real escapes live there \u2014 the true number is higher. Its report header is also hardcoded to name development-harness regardless of which plugin was scanned. Both are tracked separately.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the rule is documented at plugins/plugin-creator/docs/runtime-environment.md. That document is itself exempt from the check it defines, because the scanner skips fenced blocks and the document's worked examples are fenced; whether that exemption is correct is worth confirming during grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Repo-wide runtime escape sweep, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ed8b93ed4525caf15e9fd72f449f57eddf05107cb0c4f0240f845b1b7b726733\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSBU4A\"}"}